# Architecture boundaries

Target layout:

- `apps/api` — Lanius HTTP API (sole business entry)
- `apps/bot` — Official QQ adapter (commands → API → text/image reply)
- `apps/web` — Next.js public site + `/admin` (current UI host; API client only)
- `packages/core` — DTOs, Zod, aliases, error codes, realm/locale
- `packages/api-client` / `packages/ui` — planned shared client + presentational UI (Next + future Tauri)
- `packages/qq-official` — QQ verify/events/send; **bot only**
- `packages/card-render` — image-mode cards; bot (MVP), optional API preview
- Later: Tauri hosts — **do not scaffold now** (`docs/TODO-TAURI.md`)

Rules:

- Put shared query contracts in `core`; do not duplicate business query logic in bot/web.
- Prefer pluggable `api-client` / `ui` over Next-only coupling in shared layers.
- `qq-official` must not be imported by `api` or `web`.
- Upstream fetch adapters belong under `apps/api` (or API-owned packages), never in web/bot.
- Keep route handlers thin; validate with Zod; map errors to stable codes + i18n keys.
